			{
				"type": "Comment",
				"start": 0,
				"end": 255,
				"data": " A `//` in a whitespace-sensitive element's attribute list runs to end of line, so the `>`\n\ttakes its own line instead of hugging the last attribute. The break lands inside the tag,\n\twhere no character is content, so the literal text is untouched. "
			},
			{
				"type": "Text",
				"start": 255,
				"end": 257,
				"raw": "\n\n",
				"data": "\n\n"
			},
			{
				"type": "Comment",
				"start": 257,
				"end": 527,
				"data": " With content, the `>` takes the next line one level in and hugs the content there, the\n\tlayout an over-width `<textarea>` already takes. The list wraps around the `//` like any\n\tother list holding one, so only a comment the author put on the tag-name line stays "
			},
			{
				"type": "Text",
				"start": 527,
				"end": 528,
				"raw": "\n",
				"data": "\n"
